<div style="background-color: #e0f2f7; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 25%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 75%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> A Walk in the Neighborhood</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> It's the Best!</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Edit classmates' written work.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write simple sentences about favorite places (e.g., 'The park is fun.'). Can edit classmates' sentences about familiar places for clarity (e.g., change 'fun park' to 'The park is fun.'). Can revise sentences to add reasons using 'because' (e.g., 'I like the park because it has swings.').</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f8ff; width: 35%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f8ff; width: 55%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f8ff; width: 10%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by showing pictures of different places in a neighborhood (e.g., a park, a street with buildings, a playground). The teacher asks students to recall their favorite places from previous lessons. "What is your favorite place in the neighborhood?" "Is it a park or a street?" Students shout out words like 'park' or 'playground'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes a simple sentence on the board about a favorite place: "The park is the best place in my neighborhood." The teacher points to 'best' and models the /b/ sound. Then, the teacher adds a reason: "The park is the best place in my neighborhood because it has big swings." The teacher highlights 'because' and explains its function. The teacher models writing clear sentences with capital letters and periods.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say 'The park is the best,' does that mean I like it a little or a lot?" (A lot!)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What word do we use to tell WHY we like something, like 'I like the park ______ it has trees'?" ('because'!)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "A Walk in the Neighborhood")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short descriptive text (2-3 sentences) titled "My Favorite Place" written on a large flashcard or projected. The text describes a fictional student's favorite place in their neighborhood, using the target grammar and vocabulary.</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example Text: "My favorite place is the Big Park. It is the best place because it has many trees and beautiful flowers. I like to play there. My friends and I often ride bikes on the path. The Big Park is very fun!"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Describing preferences ('This is my favorite.'), expressing opinions ('I like this park because it is fun.'), explaining opinions using 'because' to justify preferences in familiar contexts.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher reads the text aloud.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students identify the favorite place (e.g., "What is the favorite place?").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students point out the word 'best' and 'because' in the text.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students match a simple picture (e.g., a park with swings) to the description.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">7-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Writing)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Grammar: Superlatives ('the best'), Simple present + conjunction ('I like this park because it is fun.'), Question structure ('What is your favorite?'). Vocabulary: neighborhood, park, place, tree, flower, building, street, playground, fun, exciting, beautiful, quiet, friendly, favorite, best.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Sentence Scramble:</b> The teacher writes scrambled sentences about neighborhood places on the board (e.g., "best / park / is / the / the / in / neighborhood / my"). Students work individually or in pairs to unscramble and write the correct sentences in their notebooks. (e.g., "The park is the best in my neighborhood.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>'Because' Sentence Builder:</b> The teacher provides sentence starters and word options. Students complete sentences with 'because' and a reason. (e.g., "I like the [street/playground] because it is [quiet/fun].") Students write their completed sentences in their notebooks.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Peer Sentence Check:</b> Students exchange their notebooks with a partner. They read each other's sentences from the previous activity and underline any words they think might be missing, or if a sentence doesn't make sense. The focus is on simple clarity and completeness, not grammar correction. The teacher monitors and guides.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "A Walk in the Neighborhood")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual writing task, followed by peer editing. Students will write a short description of their favorite place in their neighborhood. This draft will then be used for the editing activity in the Assessment stage.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher instructs students: "Think about your favorite place in your neighborhood. Is it a park, a street, a building, or a playground? Why is it the best? Write 3-4 sentences about it. Remember to use 'the best' and 'because'."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students write their descriptions in their notebooks or on a separate sheet of paper.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher circulates, offering assistance with vocabulary (e.g., 'What is the word for X?') and sentence structure, encouraging them to use the target grammar and vocabulary (e.g., 'Is your park big or small?').</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">12-15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Peer editing checklist. Students use a simple checklist to edit a classmate's written work.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students exchange their written descriptions from Stage 4 with a new partner. Each student uses a simple "Editing Checklist" provided by the teacher to review their partner's work. The checklist asks questions like: "Did my friend use 'the best'?", "Did my friend use 'because' to explain?", "Does the sentence start with a capital letter?", "Does the sentence end with a period?", "Is it easy to understand?". Students circle 'Yes' or 'No' and can gently suggest changes.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (focused on peer editing):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ability to identify target grammar (superlatives, 'because') in peer's writing.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ability to identify basic writing conventions (capitalization, punctuation).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of suggested revisions for classmates' sentences.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer on a small slip of paper:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing you learned about writing better sentences today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one thing you helped your friend fix in their writing?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">8-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the easiest part about writing your description? What was the hardest part?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did checking your friend's writing help you with your own writing?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> Most students successfully used 'because' and superlatives. The peer editing process was effective in highlighting common errors like missing capitalization or punctuation. Some students struggled with forming complete sentences independently; more sentence frames or guided writing practice might be needed next time. I will continue to emphasize clarity and purpose in writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson (Lesson 5 – Mediation & Integration):</b> In the next lesson, students will consolidate their writing skills by revising their favorite place descriptions based on peer feedback, and then sharing them (mediating the information) with the class or in a creative project, further integrating their learning from this lesson.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">3-5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>